                  "value": "National Panel of Chronically ill and Disabled"
                },
                "seriesInformation": {
                  "typeName": "seriesInformation",
                  "multiple": false,
                  "typeClass": "primitive",
                  "value": "Data was collected using the Dutch National Panel of the Chronically ill and Disabled. The National Panel of the Chronically ill and Disabled is a nationwide Dutch panel, established to gather information on the consequences of chronic disease and disability from a patient perspective. The National Panel of the Chronically ill and Disabled consists of more than 4,000 people with chronic illness or physical disability. Panel members fill in questionnaires up to twice a year. In these questionnaires, participants share their experiences and opinions on health and participation related topics. \nThis dataset was used for a study on the relationship between work-related factors and adherence to treatment, which is part on a larger project on employment and medication self-management.  For more information: https://www.nivel.nl/en/our-databases-and-panels/national-panel-chronically-ill-and-disabled"
                }
              }
            ]
